WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:00.936
(lively music)

00:00:00.936 --> 00:00:03.390
- [Narrator] You are looking
at the demographic breakdown

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.180
of China and India's populations.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.230
In 1990, both countries'
demographics resembled a pyramid

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.990
which meant that there were far
more young people being born

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.550
than there were old people.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.220
But fast forward to projections for 2050

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.470
and you'll notice a dramatic change.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.440
The Chinese pyramid
narrows to resemble a shape

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.673
more like a funnel.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.460
For more than two centuries,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.340
China has had the largest
population in the world.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.910
This year, the UN said
India will take its place.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.580
India's population is
expected to keep growing

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.343
for the next four decades,

00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:41.370
peaking at nearly 1.7 billion in 2063.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.640
China's population is
projected to shrink rapidly.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.170
By the start of the next century,

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.070
India's population is expected
to be double that of China's.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.900
- All the science point

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.670
to a very challenging future
for China, demographically.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.610
- [Narrator] Here's why this
shift marks a watershed moment

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.840
for both nations

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.783
and what the change could
mean for the global economy.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.840
This year, China announced

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.680
its first population decline since 1961.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.260
In 2020, China's fertility rate

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.740
or the number of children a
woman has over her lifetime

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.670
came in at 1.3 which is one
of the lowest in the world.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.820
The roots of China's
demographic crisis can be found

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.380
in its one child policy.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.590
- The policy was designed
to keep birth low

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.340
so that China would have the opportunity

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.140
to grow its economy.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.100
It turns out, in reality,
the one child policy has

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.100
far more long lasting impacts
the policy makers intended.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.930
In a way, it worked too well.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.430
- [Narrator] Starting in 1980,

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.820
most Chinese couples were
strictly limited to one child.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.790
Despite reversing the
one child policy in 2016,

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.760
China's fertility rate
is continued to decline.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.310
- The replacement rate needed

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.790
to keep a population stable is 2.1.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.100
- [Narrator] Meaning that a
woman would need to give birth

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.250
to at least two children to
keep the population stable

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.590
and essentially replace the parents.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.960
With a fertility rate of 2.0,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.970
India's fertility rate is slightly lower

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.230
than the replacement rate.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.260
- The reason why India's
population is projected

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.190
to keep growing for several
more decades is because India,

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:26.730
unlike China, still has a
fairly large group of women

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.630
of reproductive age that's
very different from China.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.520
- [Narrator] In China,
the one child policy

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.920
produced a dramatic gender imbalance

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.340
that originated in strong
cultural and social preferences

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.750
for male children.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.576
In 2021, the number of marriage
registrations plummeted

00:02:43.576 --> 00:02:45.180
to 7.6 million,

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.430
the lowest since the government
started keeping records

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.470
in the mid 1980s.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.830
The global economy has grown
to rely on China's vast pool

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.470
of factory workers for manufactured goods

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.170
and its consumers
represent a growing market

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.660
for western-made cars and luxury goods.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.630
- A declining Chinese
population would mean

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:07.680
that there will be fewer
workers to make products

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.410
that are exported to other countries

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.660
and there will be fewer consumers,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.280
especially younger consumers,

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.030
to buy goods from other countries.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.290
- [Narrator] In the coming decades,

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.910
demographers expect China

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.730
will face a huge worker to retiree gap.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:28.730
In 2020, 14% of China's
population was over 64 years old.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.940
While in India, just 7%
of people were over 64.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.140
By 2070, nearly 59% of people in China

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.970
will be over the age of 64.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.120
While in India, only 30% of the population

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.830
will be in the same age bracket.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.770
- A larger group of retirees will mean

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.250
that younger Chinese people
will have a bigger of a burden

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.080
to support the elderly.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.410
That's especially true in the rural areas.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.340
- [Narrator] In some ways,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.740
India looks like China did 30 years ago.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.590
It has a rapidly expanding
working age population

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.890
with 610 million people under age 25

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.950
and relatively few older
people to care for.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.720
India's rising population

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.180
means it's likely to
keep its economy growing,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.770
buy more of the world's goods

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.380
and play a bigger role in global affairs.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.960
But India's rise isn't assured.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.390
- India's problem now is all about jobs.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:25.470
Yes, it does have a large
working age population

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.020
but at the same time it is struggling

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:31.440
to create jobs for its young people.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.660
- [Narrator] India is
primarily a rural nation

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.570
and still lags behind
China in urbanization.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.030
Unlike China, where
millions of migrant laborers

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.310
move to cities to work in factories,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.580
many Indians are reluctant
to leave their hometowns.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.430
India also significantly lags behind China

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.613
in terms of female labor participation.

00:04:49.613 --> 00:04:52.140
India's cultural norms
have meant that families

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.850
who can't afford to keep their daughters

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.220
and wives at home prefer to do so.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.580
- When Mao took power,
he really pushed the idea

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.620
that women is equal to men.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.453
For a long time,

00:05:02.453 --> 00:05:06.300
China's women labor participation
rate has been very high

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.960
and for India, that
seemed to be not the case.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.690
- [Narrator] Whatever happens,
the world's future population

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.000
will be tilted more
towards the Global South

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.800
and South Asia, in particular.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.290
In 2060, the three successor states

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:23.190
to pre-independence India
will have 2.3 billion people

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:27.690
versus China's 1.2 billion
guaranteeing profound changes

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.172
to the global economy.

00:05:29.172 --> 00:05:31.755
(lively music)

